# OSGI Log Message
OSGI_MSG001=CWWKE0703I: {0} {1} {2} {3}
OSGI_MSG001.explanation=An informational message was logged using the OSGi log service.
OSGI_MSG001.useraction=No action is required.

OSGI_AUDIT_MSG=CWWKE0704A: {0} {1} {2} {3}
OSGI_AUDIT_MSG.explanation=An audit message was logged using the OSGi log service.
OSGI_AUDIT_MSG.useraction=No action is required.

OSGI_WARNING_MSG=CWWKE0700W: {0} {1} {2} {3}
OSGI_WARNING_MSG.explanation=A warning message was logged using the OSGi log service.
OSGI_WARNING_MSG.useraction=See the warning message for information.

OSGI_ERROR_MSG=CWWKE0701E: {0} {1} {2} {3}
OSGI_ERROR_MSG.explanation=An error message was logged using the OSGi log service.
OSGI_ERROR_MSG.useraction=See the error message for information.

OSGI_BUNDLE_EXCEPTION=CWWKE0702E: {0}
OSGI_BUNDLE_EXCEPTION.explanation=A BundleException was thrown by the OSGi Framework.
OSGI_BUNDLE_EXCEPTION.useraction=See the exception message for information.

MESSAGE.ROUTER.INVALID.WILDCARD.MESSAGE.ID.CWWKE0710W=CWWKE0710W: The wildcard message ID {0} is not valid. The expected syntax is <prefix>*[<log-level>] or *<log-level>, where <prefix> is one or more characters and <log-level> is a single character that represents one of the following log levels: I=Info, A=Audit, W=Warning, E=Error. The <log-level> is optional when a <prefix> is specified and is required when no <prefix> is specified. The wildcard message ID can contain only one asterisk (*).
MESSAGE.ROUTER.INVALID.WILDCARD.MESSAGE.ID.CWWKE0710W.explanation=The wildcard message ID is not valid. A wildcard message ID matches a group of message IDs. It uses one of two forms. The form <prefix>*[<log-level>] matches message IDs that start with the prefix, optionally limited to one log level. The form *<log-level> matches message IDs of one log level only, regardless of prefix. The <log-level> is a single character: I=Info, A=Audit, W=Warning, E=Error. The asterisk (*) must appear only once, and it must be the last character, or the second-to-last character when it is followed by a <log-level>.
MESSAGE.ROUTER.INVALID.WILDCARD.MESSAGE.ID.CWWKE0710W.useraction=Correct the message ID so that it uses one of the following forms: <prefix>*, <prefix>*<log-level>, or *<log-level>. Remove any extra asterisks and any characters after the log level. Replace the log level with one of the following characters: I=Info, A=Audit, W=Warning, E=Error.